# Roblox Development Rules

1. When asked to add or create something, make it present and editable in Roblox Studio's edit mode. Do not create it only at play-test runtime.
2. Do not add artificial parent instances or folders. Use the natural Roblox hierarchy required by the feature.
3. When creating UI, place its functional LocalScript directly under the relevant UI instance.

Keep this file updated when the user adds a new project rule.
